    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "TheaterEvent",
      "id": "bb180021734c0f49",
      "title": "Μπουζούκια στην Πίστα |Γυάλινο Μουσικό Θέατρο",
      "description": "20 Φεβ - 28 Μαρ Μπουζούκια στην Πίστα |Γυάλινο Μουσικό Θέατρο Γυαλινο Μουσικο Θεατρο",
      "fullDescription": "The bouzouki's opening trill cuts through the murmur of the crowd, and the room shifts into a different mode. Gyalino Mousiko Theatro fills with that particular energy that only bouzoukia nights generate — anticipation for the kind of performance that connects modern Athens to its laiko roots. The pista awaits.\n\n\"Mpouzoukia stin Pista\" — Bouzoukia on the Dance Floor — delivers exactly what the title promises. This is laiko music in its natural habitat, performed for an audience that knows how to respond. The dance floor isn't metaphor; it's invitation. When the familiar songs begin, the space between listener and performer collapses.\n\nLaiko carries complex cultural weight in Greece. The music emerged from rebetiko traditions, evolved through decades of commercial development, now occupies space from high-end clubs to neighborhood gatherings. Tonight's setting at Gyalino — the Glass Musical Theater — positions the genre in a room that respects its craft while maintaining accessibility.\n\nThe crowd for bouzoukia nights has a specific character. These are Greeks who grew up with these songs, who know the words without thinking, for whom the music triggers memories of family celebrations and late summer nights. But you'll also find younger listeners discovering the tradition, absorbing the vocabulary through osmosis, learning when to sing along and when to listen.\n\nThe evening will build through the classic laiko arc. Slower songs establishing mood, tempo gradually increasing, the pista filling as inhibitions drop. By midnight the room has achieved that state where everyone's participating, where the line between stage and floor has been decisively crossed.\n\nIf you need translations to understand, if the cultural codes are unfamiliar, bouzoukia nights can feel opaque. The music speaks to those who already know the language. But if you carry Greek in your bones or want to witness the tradition at full intensity, if you've been waiting for laiko performed for an audience that can match its energy — Gyalino tonight is the place.\n\n| Info | Details |\n|------|---------|\n| **Date** | Friday, February 20, 2026 |\n| **Venue** | Gyalino Mousiko Theatro |\n| **Style** | Laiko / bouzoukia |\n| **Format** | Live performance with dance floor |\n| **Crowd** | Greek-speaking audience |\n| **Good to know** | Bouzoukia nights run late — pace yourself |\n\nBouzoukia on the pista: laiko music performed where the dance floor is the point.",
      "startDate": "2026-02-20T20:00:00+03:00",
      "endDate": null,
      "type": "theater",
      "genres": [
        "music"
      ],
      "tags": [],
